  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">23-0002568_Civic inclusion of religious and ethnic grassroot communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">23-0002568_TDI will work with religious and ethnic minority grassroots civic activists towards building their capacity in three main areas: (1) gaining knowledge about the participatory citizenship and democratic governance, and the competencies of local municipalities; (2) gaining skills on planning effective advocacy actions, targeting local municipalities needs while focusing on solving the problems faced by the most vulnerable parts of society; and (3) learning how to plan and conduct effective awareness-raising activities to promote equality and inclusion in their diverse communities. Next to that, TDI will address the problem that local officials lack knowledge and skills necessary to engage in community-centered policy design, to understand and mainstream the needs of vulnerable communities, and lack the sensitivity toward the needs of the ethnic and religious minorities.</narrative>
  </description>
